ect-link {&#xA;  display: inline-flex;&#xA;  align-items: center;&#xA;  gap: 0.5rem;&#xA;  margin-top: 1rem;&#xA;  font-size: 1.4rem;&#xA;}&#xA;&#xA;.project-link:hover {&#xA;  text-decoration: underline;&#xA;}&#xA;&#xA;/* Dark mode adjustments */&#xA;@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {&#xA;  .project-card {&#xA;    /* background: #2a2a2a; */&#xA;  }&#xA;}&#xA;&lt;/style&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;projects-grid&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;project-card&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;project-icon&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;img src=&#34;https://blog.quentinfasquel.com/images/projects/private-symbols.png&#34; alt=&#34;PrivateSymbols Icon&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;  &lt;h3 class=&#34;project-title&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/quentinfasquel/PrivateSymbols&#34;&gt;PrivateSymbols&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p class=&#34;project-description&#34;&gt;&#xA;    A macOS app like SF Symbols that lets you browse private SF Symbols. Download the app and explore Apple&#39;s hidden symbol library.&#xA;  &lt;/p&gt;</description>
